/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (The Greater Cleveland Music Census is a community-led initiative to gain a better understanding of the current needs of the Cleveland-area music community. This marks the first time in over a decade that the music community will have new data from 2,768 respondents from which to develop policy solutions and approaches. The 2023 study was led by Cleveland Rocks: Past, Present, Future and The Cleveland Independent Venue Association, with support from the Cleveland Foundation. )
/E (The Greater Cleveland Music Census is a community-led initiative to gain a better understanding of the current needs of the Cleveland-area music community. This marks the first time in over a decade that the music community will have new data from 2,768 respondents from which to develop policy solutions and approaches. The 2023 study was led by Cleveland Rocks: Past, Present, Future and The Cleveland Independent Venue Association, with support from the Cleveland Foundation. )
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
279 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Across 10 key indicator areas, Cleveland is a relatively healthy music ecosystem. The Cleveland music ecosystem is mostly balanced across creatives \(74%\), industry \(18%\), and venue/presenters \(8%\). Cleveland has a decent industry segment which offers its ecosystem a competitive advantage over places lacking this infrastructure. Increasing the venue/presenters portion slightly to support the creatives with more opportunities to perform may bring more balance.)
/E (Across 10 key indicator areas, Cleveland is a relatively healthy music ecosystem. The Cleveland music ecosystem is mostly balanced across creatives \(74%\), industry \(18%\), and venue/presenters \(8%\). Cleveland has a decent industry segment which offers its ecosystem a competitive advantage over places lacking this infrastructure. Increasing the venue/presenters portion slightly to support the creatives with more opportunities to perform may bring more balance.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
280 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Most respondents \(76%\) would like to see Cleveland create a music commission at the city or county level. The focus of such a commission would be live entertainment programming, creative grants, audience development, ecosystem support, and live entertainment-friendly regulatory improvements.)
/E (Most respondents \(76%\) would like to see Cleveland create a music commission at the city or county level. The focus of such a commission would be live entertainment programming, creative grants, audience development, ecosystem support, and live entertainment-friendly regulatory improvements.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
