323 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 851 0 R
/ActualText (Race -  Leans heavily towards White/European representation, with 86% of respondents falling into this category, consistent with trends in other cities. However, Black, African, and African American representation is 13%, below the city's general population. Hispanic representation stands at just 3%, indicating a 4% gap compared to the general population. Efforts to enhance diversity and inclusion, particularly among Black, African, African American, and Hispanic communities, are necessary for a more representative music scene.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
324 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 852 0 R
/ActualText (Age - Healthy distribution. 25-29 group is the highest segment among all respondents. 40-54 group is highest among the venue/presenter respondents. We would like to see a little higher in the 18-24 range.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
325 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 853 0 R
/ActualText (Experience - Across all respondents, 7% report having less than three years of experience in the music industry. While the industry sector displays a more balanced distribution of experience levels, the creative sector is less so, with 75% boasting over 10 years of experience. Overall, this indicates a level of sustainability within the ecosystem, although efforts are needed to ensure a more equitable distribution of opportunities for emerging talent.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
